<body> 
<div>
 Hello {{lead.First Name:default= Friend}}, 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 I hope your spring semester is off to a wonderful start! As we approach the end of the year and holiday season, I’m reaching out on behalf of Flywire to personally invite you to an exclusive 
<a href="https://more.flywire.com/FlywireHosted_EDU_BOSTONCFODinner_December2024_2.RegistrationPage.html"><strong>CFO roundtable networking dinner</strong></a> on Tuesday, February 11th, focused on “Innovative Approaches to Revenue Generation and Student Affordability.” 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 As a valued Flywire client, your institution has been at the forefront of creating exceptional financial experiences for students and their families. Flywire has had the pleasure of working closely with your student financial services team. We believe there’s an opportunity to further connect and share ideas on how you can continue driving value at your institution, specifically from a CFO perspective. 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 This intimate gathering has been curated for a select group of Boston-area higher ed CFOs and senior financial leaders to foster an open dialogue around the key issues impacting our sector.&nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 Join us to network with peers and Flywire executives, including 
<strong>President and COO Rob Orgel</strong>—former Head of Apple Pay at Apple, and 
<strong>CFO Cosmin Pitigoi</strong>—a global payments expert who spent nearly 20 years at PayPal. This dinner presents a unique opportunity for you to engage with industry leaders who have been at the helm of transformational change in finance and payments. 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 Our conversation will cover: 
</div> 
<ul> 
<li><strong>Aligning Financial Leadership with Institutional Goals:</strong> The CFO’s role in advancing institutional success and sustainability&nbsp;</li> 
<li><strong>Driving New Revenue Streams:</strong> Innovative strategies for generating revenue through partnerships and technology</li> 
<li><strong>Supporting Student Affordability:</strong> How technology helps enable efficiencies from recruitment to retention</li> 
</ul> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div> 
<strong>Event Details:</strong> 
</div> 
<div> 
<strong>Date</strong>: February 11, 2024 
</div> 
<div> 
<strong>Time</strong>: 6:00 PM – 9:00 PM 
</div> 
<div> 
<strong>Location</strong>: 
<a href="https://www.gordonramsayrestaurants.com/en/us/ramsays-kitchen/locations/boston">Ramsay's Kitchen</a>&nbsp; 
<br>(774 Boylston St, Boston, MA 02199) 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 We are inviting a small group of respected leaders, and I hope you’ll be able to join us for what promises to be a thought-provoking evening. I would love to have your voice at the table as we shape this important conversation together. Seats are limited for this intimate invite-only gathering. 
<strong>Please let me know if you can attend by January 31st</strong>&nbsp;and if you’d be interested in leading a discussion topic. 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div>
 Best! 
</div> 
<div>
 &nbsp; 
</div> 
<div> 
